  "result": "Excellent! All 144 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented VAT (Value Added Tax) calculations for invoices:\n\n**1. Added `lineVAT` function** (`src/invoices.js`):\n   - Calculates VAT per line on the discounted amount\n   - Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 (vatRate / 100)`, rounded per line\n   - Clamps negative values to 0\n\n**2. Updated `invoiceTotals`**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - VAT is the sum of all line VATs\n   - Total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n   - Key principle: VAT is computed per line, never as a percentage of invoice total\n\n**3. Updated `renderInvoiceText`** (`src/render.js`):\n   - Shows Subtotal when there's discount or VAT\n   - Shows Discount line when applicable\n   - Shows VAT line just above Total (when applicable)\n   - Format: Invoice number/DRAFT \u2192 Customer name \u2192 Line items \u2192 Subtotal \u2192 Discount \u2192 VAT \u2192 Total\n\n**4. Comprehensive test coverage** (144 tests, all passing):\n   - `lineVAT` calculates correctly on original and discounted amounts\n   - Handles VAT at 0%, 9%, and 21% rates\n   - Rounds to nearest cent per line\n   - Sums VAT across multiple lines correctly\n   - Total calculation: subtotal - discount + vat\n   - Clamping prevents negative totals\n   - Render output displays all components correctly\n   - Updated existing tests to work with VAT\n\n**Design principle implemented**: VAT is computed per line on the post-discount amount and rounded individually, then the rounded line VATs are summed for the invoice VAT\u2014never computed as a percentage of the invoice total. This is the standard accounting practice and ensures correct rounding behavior.",
